WEBVTT

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:20.620
Dragonic Overlord was defeated 
from Blaster Blade's hit.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.620
I have now returned to merely a spirit.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.000
And I will be extinguished 
off the planet Cray...

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:29.630
I have lost.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.800
Aichi!

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.100
Aichi!

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.210
Aichi!

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.530
I'm...

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:21.030
Good morning...

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:25.230
Why do I always have to wake you up?

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.320
Sorry...

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.750
Honestly...

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.530
Have some breakfast, Aichi.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.760
Thanks, Emi.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:39.850
Whatever, just hurry up and eat.

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.330
You'll be late.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:57.280
Welcome to Card Capital!

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.180
Aichi!

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.090
It's time to go to school!

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:14.470
Aichi?

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.330
Okay, I'm heading out!

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.150
Huh?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.440
Aichi's started going to 
school earlier lately...

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.480
But he always used to lie around in 
his room until I yelled at him...

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.530
Now that I think about it, he's been 
coming home late more often as well.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.080
I wonder if he's found something 
fun to do at school?

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.640
At school?

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.950
Oopsie!

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.310
Emi!

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.890
Shouldn't you be heading out?

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.340
You're going to be late.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.140
See you later!

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:23.240
Seems the same to me...

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.260
Emi!

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.320
Good morning!

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.950
Oh, Mai! Good morning.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.310
Something the matter?

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.120
No, it's nothing.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.000
Hey, about yesterday's homework...

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.090
You mean observing the ecology of insects?

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:41.190
I really don't like bugs...

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.700
So I was thinking, the two of us could...

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.240
He...

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:46.020
Something the matter?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.750
No...

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:48.790
Let's go!

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:49.580
Sure...

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.580
What's up, Aichi?

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:56.980
Good morning...

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.900
We're racin' to the school!

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.460
Eat my dust!

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.110
But that's just crazy!

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:13.130
A great number of famous literary figures 
appear during this era of Japan...

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.910
These will do nicely...

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:21.020
Goodbye.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.830
See you tomorrow, Emi!

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:24.120
Yeah! See you!

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:36.890
Now that I think about it, he's been 
coming home late more often as well.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:41.440
I wonder if he's found something 
fun to do at school?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:44.280
Coming home late...

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.100
What am I going to do with him?

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:54.100
If Aichi gets home later than 
dinner, Mom'll be worried.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:57.850
Seriously?

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.800
Like, for real, man!

00:06:00.530 --> 00:06:03.460
Hey, wasn't that a Miyaji Academy uniform?

00:06:05.390 --> 00:06:06.880
That's a school for super-rich girls!

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.490
I wonder if she's a fan of mine?

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:09.090
As if!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:16.530
Oh? This school doesn't have a 
security guard at the gate...

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:18.850
Aichi!

00:06:20.470 --> 00:06:22.830
Yo, Aichi, wait up!

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.190
We're not goin' straight home today, got it?

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.740
Morikawa?

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:33.030
Hey, man, don't just go home 
without sayin' anything.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:35.360
Why don't you stop by <i>that place</i> today, huh?

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.700
Huh? Uh... right...

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.460
Aichi's tangled up with some bad people?

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.130
Yeah... You'd better show up.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.930
Because today I'm gonna show 
you just how strong I am!

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.180
You'd better be prepared, Aichi.

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.410
You want to go another 
round with me, Morikawa?

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.850
What, you're sayin' I don't satisfy ya?

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.910
No, that's not exactly what I meant...

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.800
Well then, it's settled.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:04.010
Alrighty then, off we go!

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:05.420
Let me have a go, too!

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:08.200
Sure! Right after I let him have it good...

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.630
I don't like the sound of this...

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:13.970
I hope Aichi's okay...

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:17.340
I can't wait!

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.370
For Pete's sake!

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:20.890
Why do I have to do this?

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.490
What should I do?

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.010
He is definitely wrapped 
up with some bad folks!

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.570
How terrible!

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:00.600
We're here!

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.670
Card Capital?

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.350
What's this place?

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:16.140
Could it be where Aichi...

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.100
Hey now, Aichi...

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.930
You don't have anywhere left to run...

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:25.990
The second you set foot in 
here, your luck ran out!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:32.280
So then... How should we 
take good care of you today?

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.530
I can't leave him alone.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:50.090
Aww, but that's my card...

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.530
Ooh, that's cool!

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.460
What is this place?

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:04.840
Welcome to Card Capital.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:06.680
Little miss?

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:11.630
I am the manager of Card Capital, Nitta.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:13.960
How may I help you today?

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.870
Um... I... Um...

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.160
Could this be your first time in a card shop?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.470
Yes!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:23.820
I see.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:28.790
This is a trading card game 
shop, or TCG for short.

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:31.620
Trading card game?

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:32.380
Yes.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:35.840
They're games where you collect different 
cards and then fight one-on-one.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:39.920
It's quite a popular game type 
among children these days.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:42.870
So that's what it was...

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:46.620
Wait, are you a student of Miyaji Academy?

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.060
Yes...

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:52.940
We don't really get too many people from 
there, since it's all rich girls...

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:54.650
Um...

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:58.150
Anyway, let's show you around the shop!

00:09:58.600 --> 00:09:59.370
Sure!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.100
This is the counter.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:04.330
You buy the cards you want here.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.130
The cat sleeping there is 
the Substitute Manager.

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:10.840
The sour-faced girl sitting 
there is Misaki Tokura.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.420
Well excuse me for my face.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.710
Ooh, scary!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.810
She's my niece.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:20.120
She's always helping out here at my shop.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:21.430
Oh?

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.990
Speaking of which...

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.550
This is what's really <i>in</i> these days!

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:27.070
Vanguard!

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:34.420
Oh, that's the match area.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:37.930
That's where the card 
fighters have their fights.

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:41.370
Aichi...

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:48.010
It looks like a Vanguard cardfight 
is just about to start!

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:50.120
The best part about Vanguard, you see...

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:56.970
You ready, Aichi?

00:10:57.690 --> 00:10:58.420
Yeah!

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:08.520
Alrighty then! Today I'm 
gonna show you who's boss!

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.060
Do it, do it!

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:13.440
Stand up!

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.240
Stand up!

00:11:46.150 --> 00:11:49.650
My deck is super-powerful, as usual!

00:11:49.910 --> 00:11:52.560
Just you wait, Aichi! You'll 
be through before you know it!

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:55.730
I'll take my turn now.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:01.910
I ride Marron.

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:10.740
It's your turn, Morikawa.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:11.530
Right.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:15.670
Okay, lookin' good!

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:19.610
On top of Undeux, I ride 
the super-strong Bahr!

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:25.470
And now I do a super-strong attack!

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:28.560
Um... I guard with Elaine.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:32.870
Check for a drive trigger...

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:41.560
You're one lucky dude, Aichi...

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:46.220
But even if you take good 
care of that grade 1 card,

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:49.280
it'll never be able to 
beat my super-strong deck!

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:53.210
Next time it's my turn, 
things are gonna get real!

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:55.670
Right. Here I go.

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:01.790
Oh, geez...

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:05.050
That guy in front's got 
some balance issues...

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:10.120
Are you interested in Vanguard?

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:12.340
Do you know what you'd like to do?

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:14.900
No... Not at all.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.680
I really just don't understand...

00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:17.980
I see.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:21.320
Don't worry, you'll remember 
the rules in no time.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:26.210
That's right! How about after this, 
I give you some private lessons?

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:27.510
No getting carried away.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:31.400
If you want to learn, just ask.

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:32.280
Right.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:37.460
Let's go.

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:43.550
That's...

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:46.260
Stand up, my avatar!

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:48.020
Ride!

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:49.550
Blaster Blade!

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.910
I've never seen Aichi like that...

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:05.840
Next, I call Wingal.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:08.490
Also, I call two Gallatins!

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:16.670
What's this?

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:20.960
No matter how many of those piddly little 
grade 2s you call, it won't scare me!

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:25.510
If I can put out these grade 3 
units, there's no way I'll lose!

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:29.010
Now, I attack Bahr with Gallatin!

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.020
That's only 1 damage.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:42.260
Next, I support Blaster Blade 
with Wingal and attack Bahr!

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:49.990
When Wingal supports Blaster Blade, 
it gains an additional 4000 power!

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:54.810
Check for a drive trigger!

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.070
We're not done yet!

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:05.530
And now, attack with Gallatin once again.

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:08.590
Come on, Morikawa...

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:10.400
Why aren't you guarding?

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:13.070
Idiot! Look at my hand!

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.430
They're all grade 3?

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:24.220
I didn't stick any boring guards you 
could guard with in my deck, you see!

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.780
My turn is over now.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:32.890
All right!

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:35.130
Here it comes! It's my turn!

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:37.040
Time to make my comeback!

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:38.790
Super-strong draw!

00:15:42.130 --> 00:15:43.630
Hey, Morikawa?

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:51.670
Until you get a grade 2, it doesn't 
matter how many grade 3s you have...

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.760
Why am I so unlucky?

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:57.760
Why does the god of fate 
play with me like this?

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:00.770
Is he jealous of me?!

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:03.810
It's not an issue with the god of luck...

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:12.650
In Vanguard, it's necessary to power 
up in order from grade 0 to grade 3.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:16.390
So if you don't have any grade 2 cards, 
your best ones will go to waste.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.980
I call the super-strong Bahr!

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:30.380
Even if my luck is bad, I'll show 
you how super-strong my brains are!

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:31.760
Here I go!

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:36.210
I support Bahr with the super-strong 
Bahr, and do a super-strong attack!

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:39.990
Is there a drive trigger?

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.000
No trigger...

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:45.890
But I got another grade 3!

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:52.680
How do you like my super-strong 
attack, Blaster Blade?

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:55.420
Um... I guard with Flogal.

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:10.630
How dare you!

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:11.460
Why?

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:16.060
Why do I always have such terrible luck?

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:16.980
Noob.

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:23.320
Well, I can understand the 
impulse of people like him

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.590
to just make decks with the strongest cards.

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.870
All right... It's my turn, right?

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:35.660
Then, I attack Bahr with Gallatin!

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.520
Strange...

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:46.350
When I see the two of them 
playing that game in this shop,

00:17:46.350 --> 00:17:49.470
they look like completely different people.

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:51.600
The first time I saw him,

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:55.010
all I could see was a powerful 
and scary bad person.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.330
But now he seems so small.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.340
And...

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:03.020
I-I draw for a damage trigger...

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:07.060
He picked up Tahr. That'll work!

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:12.000
Okay then. Finally a 
super-strong draw I can use!

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:18.150
Aichi, who's always trembling in fear...

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:23.020
Aichi, who wouldn't even go to 
school until I told him to...

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:28.780
He looks so much bigger than he used to.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:34.310
Next, I support Blaster Blade 
with Wingal and attack Bahr!

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:37.980
And, the thing that changed Aichi...

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:41.720
I'm sure it's that card game.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:44.300
Vanguard...

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:49.130
I won't let that through, Aichi!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:53.660
I guard your attack with 
the super-strong Tahr!

00:18:53.660 --> 00:18:56.310
10000 plus 8000 equals 18000!

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:59.500
Your attack won't go through!

00:18:59.940 --> 00:19:01.810
Uh... But...

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:02.910
What is it?

00:19:03.390 --> 00:19:04.160
See?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:08.160
When Blaster Blade is supported by Wingal,

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:12.640
its power is 13000, 9000 plus 4000.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:15.880
Then when you add in Wingal's 
own power of 6000...

00:19:16.680 --> 00:19:18.550
19000 total, yeah...

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:19.910
Plus...

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.710
What?

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.150
We turn over a card for a drive trigger...

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:29.840
Epona?! That's a critical trigger!

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:32.450
Power +5000.

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.950
And damage +1!

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.330
That's 6 damage.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.750
It's over...

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:01.730
I... lose!

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:06.750
Yeah, no kidding. Aichi has no damage!

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:08.120
What?!

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:11.820
You're right! What's the meaning of this?!

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.800
Damn it!

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.080
Why do I have such crappy luck?

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:19.960
Aichi!

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:23.990
Emi!

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:27.020
Oh? You know him?

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:29.580
A friend? Or maybe...

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.060
Um... She's my...

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:36.290
So the reason you've been coming home 
late is because you've been going here?

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.710
Y-Yeah...

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:50.930
This is Vanguard...

00:20:51.470 --> 00:20:53.040
And this is...

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:54.770
Blaster Blade.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.020
Stand up, my avatar!

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:01.300
Ride! Blaster Blade!

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:11.320
This is what you've been doing.

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:13.420
Emi, um...

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:17.040
Aichi, you've changed a little.

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.710
Is it really that fun?

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:21.870
Yeah.

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:25.260
Which one is the real one?

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:29.400
The Aichi that's here 
now, or the Aichi I know?

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:30.400
Girlfriend? Naw, couldn't be...

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:32.220
I told you, she's my sister.

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:33.460
Right...

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.770
Would you play again for me?

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:40.690
It's fun, right? Do it again!

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:43.440
Uh... Well...

00:21:45.430 --> 00:21:46.800
Alrighty then!

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.200
This time I'm gonna show you 
what I'm really made of!

00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:53.180
